course: dictionary
lesson: 7904
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues in the sentence show you which meaning the writer chose. «A giant snail rasps through cucumber with a tongue of thousands of tiny teeth.» The snail is eating, so rasps must mean scrapes its food away.
explain: «In the elephant house, keepers trim its toenails with a big rasp.» Look at the words around rasp: trim and toenails. A rasp here is a tool, a coarse file. Same word, different meaning, because the context is different.
explain: A rasp can also be a harsh sound, like a rough, scraping voice. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably chosen the right meaning.
fact: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one to use.
fact: «Rasp» can be a noun: a rough, harsh sound, or a coarse file for shaping wood or metal.
fact: «Rasp» can be a verb: to speak in a rough, harsh voice, or to scrape with a rough tool.
fact: «A giant snail rasps through cucumber» means the snail scrapes its food with its tiny teeth.
fact: A snail's radula is a ribbon covered in thousands of tiny teeth, which rasps food like a file.
exercise: «A giant snail rasps through cucumber.» What does rasps mean here? | Hides under a leaf | *Scrapes through with tiny teeth | Says something in a rough voice | Sings a happy tune
exercise: «In the elephant house, keepers trim its toenails with a big rasp.» What is a rasp in this sentence? | A kind of cucumber | *A rough tool, like a file | A type of warm sand | A loud, harsh sound
exercise: Ben says, «His rasping voice made everyone go quiet.» What does rasping voice mean? | A soft, sweet voice | A voice that sings in tune | *A rough, harsh voice | A voice speaking another language
test: Which sentence uses rasp as a verb? | *She rasped the wood smooth with a tool | A rasp is a kind of file | The rasp was sharp and rusty | He used a rasp to shape the stool
test: Which meaning fits «The old man let out a rasp of a laugh»? | A coarse tool for wood | A giant snail | A soft whisper | *A rough, harsh sound
exam: Which meaning of rasp fits «She trimmed the hoof with a rasp»? | A tiny tooth | *A coarse file, a tool | To sing softly | A harsh, rough voice
